<h3>Scoring rubric you can use</h3>

<p>Define three scores per question.</p>

<p><strong>Correctness (0/1):</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>1 if the answer matches the ground truth fact(s).</li>
  <li>0 otherwise.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Citation precision (0/1):</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>1 if the citation points to the evidence block that contains the supporting fact.</li>
  <li>0 otherwise.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Faithfulness (0/1):</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>1 if every claim in the answer is supported by retrieved evidence.</li>
  <li>0 if the answer includes unsupported claims.</li>
</ul>

<p>Then compute:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Correctness@N: average correctness across questions.</li>
  <li>CitationPrecision@N: average citation precision.</li>
  <li>Faithfulness@N: average faithfulness.</li>
</ul>

<p>You can also compute a combined metric like:</p>

<pre><code>                                                Q
EvidenceScore =  1/ Q  ∑   (Correctness i ×CitationPrecision i ×Faithfulness i )
                                               i=1</code></pre>

<p>This metric penalizes answers that are correct but uncited, or cited but unsupported.</p>

