<h2>19. Conclusion</h2>
<p>Turning scanned documents into citation-ready Markdown is the highest-leverage upgrade you can make for scanned-document RAG. The goal is not just to extract text; it is to preserve evidence relationships and attach stable provenance so retrieval returns the right context and citations remain trustworthy.</p>
<p>If you build OCR-to-Markdown with deterministic structure assembly and evidence-block provenance, your RAG system stops guessing and starts citing.</p>
